	abstract = {In this video, we explore the fascinating concept of Noether's theorem, which explains the relationship between symmetry and conservation laws in physics. We discuss how every continuous symmetry of a physical system has a corresponding conservation law, and give examples of these in action, such as the conservation of momentum and angular momentum. We also explore the various applications of Noether's theorem in real-world systems, from rockets launching into space to subatomic particles colliding in particle accelerators. Join us on this journey of discovery and learn how Noether's theorem has transformed the field of physics.emmy noether},
